From 88ddcb0278bf18a85e9fada0842e906f3faecbd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:55:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 49/97] vulkan: per-draw CPU cost - sampler parameter/usage
 memos and a 16-entry texture descriptor set cache

Live draw-stage timing (Linux, keep-60 entrances, rdtsc per IssueDraw stage): ~1050 ns/draw; bindings 258,
render-target cache 135, vertex buffers/barriers/emit 113, samplers 105, primitive processing 104, textures 98.
Laptop heavy entrances: ~12k draws/frame at ~1.28 us/draw.

- GetSamplerParameters: memo per fetch constant slot keyed by the raw 6 fetch dwords, the binding's filter
  overrides and anisotropic_override (max_anisotropy_ is fixed) - a pure function of those.
- UseSampler: samplers already used in the current submission are returned without the map lookup/LRU update
  (a sampler used in the current submission can't be evicted before it completes).
- Texture descriptor sets: reuse by content among the last 16 sets per stage within the submission (was: only
  the previous draw's); hashed image infos; same validity rules and invalidation. A hit on a set other than the
  bound one clears its bound flag (first version missed this and bound stale textures - caught by image A/B).

Replay A/B (2 heavy entrance traces x300, 3 alternating rounds): -1.7% and -1.0% frame time (about half of it is
trace decompression), images pixel-identical to the previous binary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
